attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 27, `nudK` to `yfeX`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 17% of calls {S1}. The model names 86 to 99.6% of them, fewest at column 17, `eutB`, 86% {S1}.

@variable **A variable column breaks the spine at 28**, `pbp4b`, carried by 76% {S2.c28}. The `eut` genes, columns 5 to 21, are [[ethanolamine utilization microcompartment]], and the `cys` genes, columns 33 to 37, are [[sulfate thiosulfate transport]] {S1, S5, Q}. The most plastic stretch is columns 50 to 55, variable, in a region of plasticity in 28 to 57% of calls {S6, P}.

@model **The model names about as many genes on the spine columns as on the fork and variable ones**, 94 against 92%, and hesitates less there, 0.26 against 0.33 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 17, `eutB`, is a spine column, at 1.35 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 69 to 79, `ypdE` to `yfdX`, are carried by 76 to 90% of chromosomes, all persistent {S10}. The last column is `yfdX`, in 76% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 93% of genes**, 0.28 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.17 against 0.21 bits, and names fewer genes, 77% against 95% {C}.

